 Day 5 — Azure DevOps CI/CD + Pipelines Architecture

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your team needs end-to-end CI/CD for a microservices application. How will you design Azure DevOps Pipelines for build, test, and deployment?

2️⃣ A pipeline must deploy to Dev → QA → Prod with manual approval gates. How will you implement this in Azure DevOps?

3️⃣ Your build pipeline is slow due to repeated dependency downloads. How will you optimize pipeline performance?

4️⃣ Secrets are hardcoded in pipeline YAML files. How will you redesign secret management securely?

5️⃣ A deployment to production failed due to a bad release. How will you design rollback and safe release strategies?

6️⃣ Multiple teams are working on the same repo but need different pipelines. How will you manage pipeline isolation and permissions?

7️⃣ You need infrastructure provisioning as part of CI/CD. How will you integrate Terraform or ARM/Bicep with Azure DevOps?

8️⃣ A pipeline must deploy containers to AKS. How will you design authentication and authorization securely?

9️⃣ You want GitOps-style deployments instead of push-based CD. How will you implement this on Azure?

🔟 Your pipeline should run only when specific folders change. How will you configure triggers and conditions?

1️⃣1️⃣ You need quality gates like code coverage and static analysis before merge. How will you integrate this into Azure DevOps?

1️⃣2️⃣ A self-hosted agent is required due to network restrictions. How will you design and manage it securely?

1️⃣3️⃣ You must enforce environment-specific configurations without duplicating pipeline code. How will you design reusable templates?

1️⃣4️⃣ Audit and traceability are required for every deployment. How will you design logging and approvals in pipelines?

1️⃣5️⃣ CI/CD must support multi-region deployments for DR readiness. How will you design the pipeline strategy?
